.TH CVECTOR_CREATE 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cvector_create \- create a vector with default memory management
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvec cvector_create(size_t elem_size, char **err);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Creates a new vector for elements of the given size. It starts with the
minimum capacity of 4 elements and resizes itself as needed, using the
standard malloc and free for its memory.

It is a static inline wrapper around cvector_create_full() that passes
NULL for the memory management procedures.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
elem_size  Size of each element in bytes (must be > 0, and must not
           exceed SIZE_MAX / 4)
err        Optional pointer that receives an error string on failure
           (pass NULL to ignore it)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the new vector on success.
NULL on failure, with the error string set in *err if err was given.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The initial capacity is 4 elements. The capacity doubles when the vector
is full and halves when it is less than 1/4 full.

Destroy the vector with cvector_destroy() when you are done with it.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_create_full (3),
.BR cvector_destroy (3),
.BR cvec_construct (3)
